# The attack trigger has a target requirement: with only Llanowar Elves (a Druid) attacking there is no legal target, so the
# trigger is not put on the stack (the bare Target refusal) and nothing explores; the Dungeoneer stays home. (The library
# is all Lightning Bolts because the venture's land search shuffles it. The initiative's venture in turn 3's upkeep
# puts the Forge's counters on the Dungeoneer, so the Elves' 1 damage is all Bot2 takes.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Swamp
Mox Emerald
Seasoned Dungeoneer
Llanowar Elves
Island
Island
Lightning Bolt x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Seasoned Dungeoneer.Cast
Bot1.Search()
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot1.Modes(Forge)
Bot1.Target(Seasoned Dungeoneer)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves)
! Bot1.Target
! Bot1.Arrange
! Bot1.Choose
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Library.Count = 11
Bot1.Battlefield.Seasoned Dungeoneer.Tapped = false
